PATCH 505: the mirrored transparency-sprite pair 2a39 / 2a7a -- FUN_0000_2ae9 / FUN_0000_2b1e's twins.

FUN_0000_2a39 (asm 0x2a39-0x2a79) is structurally FUN_0000_2ae9 (patch 312): resolve the sprite through
260c, then split on the returned flags --
    2a3a: 8b 3e 24 07  mov di,[0x724] ; 2a3e: call 0x260c ; 2a41: jb 0x2a78 ; 2a43: jne 0x2a6d
    ZF=1: push si/es ; mov bx,0x1588 ; call 0x2d6d ; movw [0x794],0x7c8 ; movw [0x796],0x140 ;
          pop es/si ; mov di,[0x1588] ; mov dx,[0x158e] ; xor cx,cx ; call 0x2a7a ; call 0x2e12
    ZF=0: mov di,cx (260c's CX) ; mov dx,[0x158e] ; xor cx,cx ; call 0x2a7a
Ghidra used the always-false `in_CF`/`in_ZF` flag artifacts, so it took the CF==0 path unconditionally,
gated the 2d6d branch on the wrong flag, called 2a7a ONCE for both branches with the wrong DI, and passed
the source pointer as a raw parameter instead of the ES:SI that 260c publishes (m_260c_recseg/recoff,
patch 114; m_260c_cx, patch 303).

FUN_0000_2a7a (asm 0x2a7a-0x2ae8) is FUN_0000_2b1e (patch 446) with the destination cursor walking
BACKWARDS -- `stos al` followed by `sub di,2`, and `dec di` on a transparent byte, both a net -1 with the
write at the pre-decrement DI:
    2a7a: mov ax,es                     ; the SOURCE segment 260c left in ES:SI
    2a7c: add di,di ; add di,[0x794] ; mov di,[di] ; add di,dx ; dec di
    2a87: mov bp,[0x724] ; mov es,[bp+0] ; mov bp,[bp+4] ; xor bp,cx ; sub bp,cx
    2a95: push ds ; mov ds,ax
    2a98: mov cx,[si-4] ; xor dx,dx ; xchg dl,cl ; xchg cl,ch    ; cx = rows (hi byte), dx = cols (lo)
    2aa1: cmpb [si-2],2 ; je 0x2ac3
    plain (0x2aa7): per row `lodsb; or al,al; je -> dec di; else stos al; sub di,2`, then
                    `add di,dx ; add di,bp`
    RLE   (0x2ac3): per row save DI in DX, `lodsb; sub di,ax` (skip), `lodsb; mov cx,ax` (run), the same
                    transparent-byte loop, then `mov di,dx ; add di,bp`
Ghidra base-lost all three bases -- the [0x794] row table (read as a host `int *`), the [0x724]
framebuffer descriptor (`mov es,[bp+0]` / `mov bp,[bp+4]`, both SS=DGROUP-relative) and the source
segment carried in ES -- and used the source parameter as a raw host pointer.  Rebuilt in patch 446's
style with 16-bit real-mode wrap on BOTH the source and destination offsets.

This pair is the top SIGSEGV of the post-494 combat cascade: with the AI actually firing, the
player-death cockpit repaint reaches it via 2a7a <- 2a39 <- 8682 <- 7fc7.
